%erg 0.1
Title: erg migrate: fold wrapped log details and normalize date-only timestamps
Created: 2026-06-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-03T19:54Z claude created

--- body ---
## Source
0216 dogfood migration, 2026-06-03. Two of the six migrated stores
(cadens: 29 files, Climate_finance: 7 files) needed the same one-off
Python script after `erg migrate` ran clean -- the legacy pattern is
common enough to absorb into migrate itself.

## Context
`%erg v1`-era stores wrote log entries as a timestamped line followed by
free-form block content: indented wrap continuations, unindented prose
paragraphs, numbered lists, blank-line-separated paragraphs -- even
whole review documents. They also wrote date-only stamps
(`2026-04-23 claude ...` without `THH:MMZ`). All of these are
malformed-log-line violations under %erg 0.1, and migrate currently
leaves them: a store can exit `erg migrate` still failing validation.

That breaks migrate's implicit contract ("after migration, erg validate
will reject any REMAINING legacy lines" reads as: format legacies are
gone). It also defeats the per-file pre-commit validate on any repo
that installs hooks after migrating.

## Fix
Two new idempotent migrate rules, same spirit as the interior-blank
sweep (accept on read, autofix on write), applied inside the log
section only:

1. Fold: any line that does not start with a `YYYY-MM-DD` timestamp is
   joined (single-space, stripped) onto the preceding entry's line.
   Blank lines between an entry and its continuation content are
   dropped. Content before the first timestamped entry is left
   untouched (still a violation -- it has no parent entry; do not guess).
2. Stamp: a leading `YYYY-MM-DD ` (date, no time) is rewritten to
   `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00Z ` -- the conventional date-only normalization.

Reference behaviour: the throwaway normalizer used in the 0216 run
(joined 29 cadens + 7 Climate_finance files; full corpus validate PASS
after). Content is preserved verbatim modulo whitespace joins.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg migrate` on a fixture with wrapped details, unindented
      paragraphs, numbered lists, blank separators, and date-only
      stamps produces a store where `erg validate` passes on every file
- [ ] Idempotent: second run byte-identical (byte-compare, not counts)
- [ ] Orphan content before the first log entry is NOT folded and still
      reported by validate
- [ ] migrate summary line reports the two new rewrite counts
- [ ] make check passes
